WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.269
PTP

00:00:01.435 --> 00:00:02.944
previous-token prediction

00:00:02.756 --> 00:00:04.312
for black-box LLM

00:00:04.124 --> 00:00:05.515
prompt reconstruction

00:00:06.054 --> 00:00:07.127
A paper trains

00:00:06.938 --> 00:00:08.129
an inverse language

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:09.155
model from scratch

00:00:09.403 --> 00:00:10.700
using previous-token

00:00:10.512 --> 00:00:11.726
prediction on data

00:00:11.538 --> 00:00:12.504
generated by the

00:00:12.316 --> 00:00:13.589
target LLM

00:00:13.778 --> 00:00:15.146
to reconstruct prompts

00:00:14.957 --> 00:00:16.384
from responses without

00:00:16.196 --> 00:00:17.598
weights or logits

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:19.780
Prior LLM inversion

00:00:19.592 --> 00:00:20.688
work treats prompt

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.009
recovery as semantic

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:22.787
reconstruction

00:00:22.965 --> 00:00:24.568
fine-tuning seq2seq

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:25.594
models on large

00:00:25.441 --> 00:00:26.950
external datasets and

00:00:26.797 --> 00:00:27.893
often needing weights

00:00:27.705 --> 00:00:28.695
or logits

00:00:29.222 --> 00:00:31.061
PTP instead mirrors

00:00:30.873 --> 00:00:32.134
next-token prediction

00:00:32.382 --> 00:00:33.431
the inverse model

00:00:33.243 --> 00:00:34.351
learns to generate

00:00:34.163 --> 00:00:35.401
the prompt backwards

00:00:35.213 --> 00:00:36.273
from the response

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.500
trained only on

00:00:37.312 --> 00:00:38.856
synthetic prompt /

00:00:38.668 --> 00:00:40.082
response pairs from

00:00:39.894 --> 00:00:41.002
the target model

00:00:41.526 --> 00:00:42.540
Full story on

00:00:42.351 --> 00:00:43.247
the dashboard
